      "content": "Thanks, that's much better and more helpful for my lesson plan. \n\nCould you finish the last sentence? You were talking about the yield of the reaction. Also, I'm particularly interested in the \"suddenness\" of the sensation. Even though the chemical reaction is happening, it feels like there's a mischievous or aggressive quality to how quickly the sting hits the eyes—it's almost like the irritation is \"attacking\" you. From a kinetic or physical standpoint, what is it about the volatility or the diffusion of the propanethial S-oxide that makes the onset feel so sharp and unexpected?",
